-- UNTESTED. DO NOT TRUST UNTIL IT HAS RUN ON RELEASE DAY.
--
-- The table dr3_neighbourhood does not exist before DR4 is released (Wednesday
-- 2 December 2026, about 12:00 CET). This query is written from section 7.3 of ESA's draft
-- DR4 data model (the PDF inside
-- https://anonftp.cosmos.esa.int/pub/GAIA_PUBLIC_DATA/Gaia_DR4/dr4-prerelease/gaia-dr4-prerelease-draft-data-model_2026-06-26.zip,
-- read on 27 Oct 2026; the zip name says 2026-06-26, the document's own front page says
-- "date: 2026-05-20, status: Draft"). ESA says the final data model may differ from the
-- draft without notice. Before running, check the table and column names against the
-- published data model.
--
-- What the draft says (section 7.3):
--   source_id                  the DR4 source ID (the key column is source_id, NOT dr4_source_id)
--   dr3_source_id              the Gaia E/DR3 source ID
--   angular_distance           mas; the DR4 position is moved to J2016.0 with the DR4 proper
--                              motion when there is one (a linear move), then compared with
--                              the DR3 position
--   magnitude_difference       DR4 G minus DR3 G, later release minus earlier release. This is
--                              the same sense as in gaiadr3.dr2_neighbourhood, where it is
--                              DR3 G minus DR2 G (checked on our 651 stars)
--   proper_motion_propagation  true if the DR4 source had a proper motion to move it with
--   probable_match             true if angular_distance < 60 mas and
--                              -0.25 <= magnitude_difference <= 0.35
--   The table lists pairs closer than 2 arcsec, for DR4 sources that already existed in DR3.
--   The draft says most sources associated with the same object "can be identified by
--   sharing the same source_id in both releases", and that different identifiers are
--   assigned in other cases. ESA's DR4 page (last updated 14 Sep 2026) says the DR4 source
--   list "should be treated as independent from Gaia DR3". Do not match by equal ID.
-- Our inference, not stated in the draft: one DR3 source can have several DR4 neighbours and
-- one DR4 source several DR3 neighbours, because the table is made of all pairs within 2
-- arcsec. The second query at the end of this file lets you check the second case.
-- The schema name of this table (gaiadr4) is also an assumption. The draft's own example
-- query reads gaiadr4.gaia_source and gaiadr3.gaia_source.
--
-- How to use: replace {ids} with up to 100 DR3 source IDs from tic_to_gaia_dr3.csv
-- (column dr3_source_id), separated by commas. release_day/dr4_link.py makes the batches.
-- Unknown before release: whether dr3_source_id is indexed in this table. If a query is
-- slow, use smaller batches and wait between jobs (5 jobs at once, 50 queued, per user).

SELECT n.dr3_source_id,
       n.source_id AS dr4_source_id,
       n.angular_distance,
       n.magnitude_difference,
       n.proper_motion_propagation,
       n.probable_match
FROM gaiadr4.dr3_neighbourhood AS n
WHERE n.dr3_source_id IN ({ids})
ORDER BY n.dr3_source_id, n.angular_distance

-- Second query, to see whether a chosen DR4 source also belongs to other DR3 sources
-- (replace {dr4_ids} with the DR4 source IDs found above):
--
-- SELECT n.dr3_source_id, n.source_id AS dr4_source_id, n.angular_distance,
--        n.magnitude_difference, n.proper_motion_propagation, n.probable_match
